# Which SSH keys git should trust for which identities, when verifying SSH
# commit signatures. Without this, git can make signatures but cannot check
# them, and %G? reports N for every commit -- including my own.
#
# Format: <principal> <keytype> <key>
# The principal is matched against the commit's author/committer email, so it
# must be the email in [user] of shared/dotfiles/.gitconfig, NOT whatever
# comment happens to be attached to the key.
#
# Only my own key is listed, so only my own commits verify. Anyone else's show
# N until their key is added here.
#
# Symlinked to ~/.ssh/allowed_signers; pointed at by gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile
# in .gitconfig.local next door. Public keys only -- nothing here is secret.
